    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for LawDog centers on the heavy offensive environment surrounding our matchup against Brandon Young. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.71) headline our starters, with **Lawrence Butler** benefiting immensely from a +10% park factor and a +13% platoon edge against the right-handed Young. Similarly, **Zack Gelof** (62.55) projects as a strong play in that same contest; while his raw base projection is modest, the combination of favorable park dynamics and Young\u2019s hittable profile provides the upside we need. **JJ Bleday** (62.12) also secures a spot, as the optimizer prioritizes his significant +14% dynamic platoon advantage against the southpaw Peterson, effectively balancing our exposure to elite arms like Skubal, who creates a tough environment for **Gleyber Torres** (52.25).\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Braden Montgomery** (45.35), who carried the highest \"near-miss\" score but ultimately lost out due to a lack of elite categorical upside compared to our starters. While **Braden Montgomery** offers a solid floor, the optimizer opted for **Dylan Beavers** (59.48), whose high projected score is anchored by an 18% skill-advantage against the left-handed Lopez. We are monitoring **Bryce Harper** (50.97) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (56.59) closely, as both are subject to pending lineup confirmations. **Jung Hoo Lee** in particular is a high-variance play; while he benefits from a +5% wind-out factor, he faces the toughest individual matchup of the day against Kohl Drake. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the scarcity of stolen bases. **Daulton Varsho** (52.83) retains his spot primarily for his defensive and situational utility, though his efficiency is hampered by a negative platoon dynamic. We are avoiding **Luis Arraez** (40.33) and **Justin Crawford** (38.06) today, as their projected outputs against Detmers fall well below our threshold; **Justin Crawford** in particular is sidelined by a projected #9 spot in the lineup. With **Will Smith** still confirmed on the IL, we will rely on the tandem of **Cal Raleigh** (46.25) and **Yainer Diaz** (43.90) to manage the catcher slot, despite **Cal Raleigh** battling a stiff test against Cease\u2019s 3.01 xERA.",
